---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const p='/equipment/05-11/';
const manual='https://www.quimica.uns.edu.ar/images/stories/descargas/Manuales%20LIUC/FTIR/FTIR%20-%20Guia%20de%20Usuario%20IR.pdf';
const spec='https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/MSD/Specification-Sheets/PS52301-nicolet-is50-ftir-spectrometer.pdf';
const gmu='https://nff.gmu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/SOP-FTIR.pdf';
const refs=[
 ['front','Front of instrument','User guide printed p. 10 shows the no-ABX base without ATR; PS52301 cover shows the distinct built-in right-side ATR station on an optioned system. This model combines documented options without the extra towers.',manual+'#page=16'],
 ['atr','Diamond ATR and pressure foot','George Mason University, Fig. 20, p. 15 shows stainless pressure assembly, diamond plate and Touch Point. Exact clearances and travel inferred.',gmu+'#page=15'],
 ['bay','Main sample compartment','User guide printed p. 11 documents opening and central bay dimensions. The side ATR station, not this chamber, is used by the experiment.',manual+'#page=17'],
 ['rear','Rear service view','User guide printed p. 27 identifies five electronics ports and their order. External screen and rear fitting dimensions illustrated, not vendor CAD.',manual+'#page=33']];
---
<Layout pageTitle="Nicolet iS50 · ATR FTIR bench" description="Acquire a simulated FTIR interferogram, recover intensity and absorbance, and compare passive polymer signatures." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment ft">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/05-11/">← Equipment 05-11</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#ft-ref">References</a><a href="#ft-tests">Verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">05-11 · INFRARED MATERIALS METROLOGY</span><h2>Nicolet iS50 FTIR</h2><p>Thermo Scientific iS50 base with the built-in single-bounce diamond ATR and pressure tower, no ABX or Raman tower. Acquire a background on the empty crystal, seat a virtual polymer coupon, then compare the recovered absorbance against three synthetic profiles.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><span class="eq-meta">01 / INSPECT</span><h3>Diamond ATR station</h3><div id="ft-model" aria-label="Orbitable Nicolet iS50 with articulated lid and ATR clamp"></div><div class="bar">{['Overall','ATR','Bay','Rear','Bench'].map(x=><button data-ft-view={x}>{x}</button>)}<button id="ft-vr" hidden>Enter VR</button></div><p id="ft-view" role="status">Loading instrument…</p><p class="small">Drag to orbit, pinch or scroll to zoom. The lid, diamond plate, pressure arm and ATR Touch Point can be clicked on the model. The main bay and the external readout are for inspection.</p></section>
<section><span class="eq-meta">02 / ACQUIRE</span><h3>Blank, coupon and settings</h3>
<div class="plan"><label>Virtual coupon<select id="ft-coupon"><option value="PMMA">PMMA-like</option><option value="PE">Polyethylene-like</option><option value="PS">Polystyrene-like</option><option value="BLANK">Clean blank</option></select></label>
<label>OPD samples<select id="ft-n"><option value="1024">1024 · 15.625 cm⁻¹ bins</option><option value="2048">2048 · 7.8125 cm⁻¹ bins</option><option value="4096" selected>4096 · 3.90625 cm⁻¹ bins</option><option value="8192">8192 · 1.953125 cm⁻¹ bins</option></select></label>
<label>Interferogram window<select id="ft-window"><option value="hann">Periodic Hann</option><option value="rect">Rectangular</option></select></label>
<label>OPD noise fraction (%)<input id="ft-noise" type="number" min="0" max=".5" step=".01" value="0"/></label>
<label>Imposed absorbance tilt<input id="ft-tilt" type="number" min="-.2" max=".2" step=".01" value="0"/></label>
<label>Baseline correction<select id="ft-baseline"><option value="none">None</option><option value="linear-ends">Line from endpoint windows</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button id="ft-power">Power on</button><button id="ft-lid">Open lid</button><button id="ft-load">Place coupon</button><button id="ft-clamp">Seat ATR foot</button></div>
<div class="bar"><button id="ft-bg">Acquire clean background</button><button id="ft-run">Acquire sample</button><button id="ft-demo" class="primary">Run PMMA-like example</button><button id="ft-process">Reprocess baseline</button></div>
<p id="ft-status" aria-live="polite">Clear the ATR crystal for background.</p>
<details><summary>Import paired spectral intensities</summary><p>Accepts <code>bts.ftir-intensity.v1</code> with ascending wavenumbers, positive background and sample intensities. Direct import bypasses the FFT and is labeled as supplied. <a href={p+'intensity-contract.json'}>Data contract</a> · <a href={p+'decade-example.json'}>Known-ratio example</a></p><input id="ft-import" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" aria-label="Paired intensity JSON"/></details></section></div>
<section><span class="eq-meta">03 / INSPECT THE RESULT</span><h3>Interferogram to absorbance</h3>
<div class="grid"><div><canvas id="ft-opd" width="720" height="265" aria-label="Sample and background interferograms versus optical path difference"></canvas><canvas id="ft-chart" width="720" height="300" aria-label="Recovered absorbance versus wavenumber"></canvas></div><div><output id="ft-results" aria-live="polite">No acquisition.</output><div class="bar"><button id="ft-json" disabled>Export absorbance (JSON)</button><button id="ft-csv" disabled>Export spectra (CSV)</button><button id="ft-intensity" disabled>Export paired intensities</button></div></div></div></section>
<section><h3>What the simulator calculates</h3>
<p>An ideal spectrum is turned into a two-sided, real interferogram by an inverse FFT. Here <em>optical path difference</em> is the optical distance imbalance, not mirror travel. The same FFT window is applied to both blank and specimen. Magnitudes are reconstructed on the positive wavenumber axis and absorbance is <strong>A = −log₁₀(S/B)</strong>. The optional baseline subtracts a line through the mean of the first and last 4% of points; it can erase genuine broad features. A normalized correlation compares the baseline-processed shape with the three teaching profiles.</p>
<p><strong>Resolution:</strong> OPD spacing is fixed at 0.0000625 cm, giving an 8000 cm⁻¹ Nyquist limit. At 4096 samples the bin pitch is 3.90625 cm⁻¹, and maximum absolute OPD is 0.128 cm. Changing the sample count changes OPD span and bin pitch. A Hann window broadens peaks and suppresses leakage. Bin pitch is not physical FWHM or instrument resolution. The displayed band is 450–4000 cm⁻¹. Sampling and noise settings invalidate the old background.</p>
<p><strong>Limits:</strong> Gaussian lines are synthetic illustrations, not measured or licensed spectra. The model does not solve evanescent-field penetration, sample force, real crystal dispersion, vendor phase correction, atmospheric gases or detectors. A synthetic-library match is not a materials identification. Imported intensities can have unverified origin. No compatible downstream ATR-spectrum station currently consumes this schema; example and contract are provided.</p></section>
<section id="ft-ref"><span class="eq-meta">04 / EVIDENCE</span><h3>Reference sheet</h3><p>Original geometry renders linked to manufacturer and institutional drawings and photographs. The exact serial revision and undocumented fixtures are not asserted.</p>
<div class="figs">{refs.map(([id,title,text,url])=><figure><img src={p+id+'.webp'} alt={'Original iS50 illustration: '+title} loading="lazy"/><figcaption><b>{title}.</b> {text} <a href={url}>Original source</a></figcaption></figure>)}</div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Specification</th><th>Value / applicability</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Legacy dimensional reference</td><td>23.745 × 28.996 × 11.653 in W/D/H (603.12 × 736.50 × 296.39 mm); tip rises to nominal 14.325 in (363.86 mm). Adopted legacy drawing. PS52301 lists a different 626 × 698 × 276 mm base; they are not treated as interchangeable geometry.</td><td><a href={manual+'#page=16'}>Guide pp. 10–11</a> · <a href={spec+'#page=2'}>PS52301</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Central sample compartment</td><td>8.12 in width, 9.94 in depth, 6.37 in height, nominal internal drawing. Not used for ATR measurement.</td><td><a href={manual+'#page=17'}>User guide p. 11</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>ATR optical option</td><td>Built-in diamond, selected mid-IR study; vendor option has wider band and multiple detector pathways. No vendor spectral performance claim.</td><td><a href={spec}>PS52301 current options</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Teaching fixture mechanics</td><td>8 mm pressure assembly lift and 1.32 rad sample hatch opening, visually inferred; not factory force or travel.</td><td><a href={gmu+'#page=15'}>GMU Fig. 20</a></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="ft-tests"><span class="eq-meta">05 / VERIFICATION</span><h3>Independent checks</h3><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>1:10 sample/background in known band</td><td>Absorbance 1 inside; 0 outside</td><td>1 / 0</td><td>10⁻¹²</td></tr>
<tr><td>Analytic cosine on FFT bin</td><td>1500 cm⁻¹, positive DFT magnitude 2048</td><td>1500 cm⁻¹ / 2048</td><td>10⁻⁹ magnitude</td></tr>
<tr><td>Clean blank repeat</td><td>No nonzero absorbance</td><td>Zero</td><td>10⁻¹²</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hann adjacent bin</td><td>0.5× center amplitude</td><td>0.5×</td><td>10⁻¹⁰</td></tr>
<tr><td>Stale background or bare clamp</td><td>Reject</td><td>Rejected</td><td>Exact</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p><a href={p+'reference-cases.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={p+'verification.json'}>Verification results</a> · <a href={p+'example-output.json'}>Example output</a> · <a href={p+'nicolet-is50.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={p+'nicolet-is50.blend'} download>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={p+'model.py'}>Generator</a> · <a href={p+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a></p><p class="small">Optional WebXR and desktop share the same state. Physical headset and instrument calibration are unverified.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/05-11/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.ft{max-width:80rem}.ft .grid,.ft .figs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.ft section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:.85rem 0;padding:.85rem 0;min-width:0}.ft h2{margin:.2em 0}.ft p{line-height:1.45}.ft .plan{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.ft label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2em;min-width:0}.ft button,.ft input,.ft select{font:inherit;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);min-height:2.4rem;border-radius:.17em;padding:.4em .5em;min-width:0;max-width:100%}.ft button{cursor:pointer}.ft button:disabled{opacity:.53;cursor:default}.ft .primary{background:#23545a;color:white}.ft .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.45rem;margin:.6rem 0}.ft #ft-model{height:clamp(280px,33vw,442px);width:100%;background:#d8dddd;touch-action:none}.ft #ft-model :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.ft canvas{width:100%;height:auto;margin-bottom:.45rem;display:block}.ft output{font-family:monospace;white-space:pre-line}.ft [hidden]{display:none!important}.ft figure{margin:0}.ft img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.ft .small,.ft figcaption{font-size:.88rem}.ft table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.9rem}.ft td,.ft th{text-align:left;padding:.45em;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.ft code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ft .scroll{overflow-x:auto}.ft #ft-status.error{color:#a74a2e}@media(max-width:800px){.ft .grid,.ft .figs{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
